      <section id="about" class="section container">
        <div class="section-heading"><span>01</span><h2>About the workshop</h2></div>
        <div class="two-column">
          <p class="lead">Artificial intelligence is reshaping how financial markets are designed, analyzed and operated. New venues, new assets and new forms of automation are opening questions at the frontier of market microstructure.</p>
          <div><p>From centralized exchanges to decentralized protocols, trading, liquidity provision, price formation and information flow remain central challenges. This workshop brings together researchers and practitioners working at the intersection of artificial intelligence and market microstructure.</p><p>Through invited talks, contributed presentations, panels and interactive sessions, the workshop will explore machine learning, reinforcement learning, agent-based modelling and other data-driven methods for modern financial systems.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="topics" class="section section-muted"><div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading"><span>02</span><h2>Topics of interest</h2></div>
        <div class="topic-list">
          <article><span>01</span><div><h3>AI agents for trading</h3><p>Learning, reasoning and acting in complex market environments.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Liquidity and market making</h3><p>Intelligent agents as providers and consumers of liquidity.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Price discovery and optimal execution</h3><p>Forecasting, routing and execution in automated markets.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>04</span><div><h3>DeFi market microstructure</h3><p>AMMs, order books, MEV, protocols and tokenized assets.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>05</span><div><h3>Risk, market design and regulation</h3><p>Robustness, surveillance and governance of AI in finance.</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </div></section>

